        "id": 13711,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-03T15:42:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was just thinking a little about our world, and how it might connect to the world of Spirit Island.</p>\n<p>In our world, there’s a misconception that native people had little or no technology. A better characterization is that native technologies developed under different pressures than European technologies - and in some cases were actually superior. To take North America as an example: moccasins, bows, and canoes were superior to boots, matchlock muskets, and dinghies in that terrain. And whenever there was a European technology that worked better, such as flintlock muskets, the natives quickly traded to get it. The cultures were much more similar in terms of pragmatism and technology than a history written by the victors suggests.</p>\n<p>This line of thought got me wondering: if the same relationships apply to the Invaders and Dahan, how much of what we know about the alternate-history development of the Dahan culture also applies to the Invaders? <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Are there spirits working with some Invader nations?</span></p>\n<p>…perhaps there’s an expansion in there, a la Pandemic’s bioterrorist!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:35.763Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
