        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>In our world, there's a misconception that native people had little or no technology....&nbsp;whenever there was a European technology that worked better, such as flintlock muskets, the natives quickly traded to get it. The cultures were much more similar in terms of pragmatism and technology than a history written by the victors suggests.</span></p></blockquote><p>Very true!</p><blockquote><p><span>...how much of what we know about the alternate-history development of the Dahan culture also applies to the Invaders?&nbsp;</span><span>Are there spirits working with some Invader nations?</span></p></blockquote><p>For now, I'm going to put on my Inscrutiable Hat and say neither \"yes\" nor \"no\" but simply \"the answer to that question is known\".</p>",
